{%- comment -%}
  One media item's colour tags, as a "Value||Value||" string.

  Extracted because the gallery stage and the thumbnail rail need the SAME
  answer for the same media and carried two byte-identical copies of this
  parser inline. It returns a value by being rendered inside a capture, then
  stripped — see the two call sites in snippets/pdp-gallery.liquid.

  The strip is not optional: render inherits this file's own whitespace, and
  theme.js compares the pieces of data-colors to option values with ===, so a
  single leading space turns " Pink" into a colour that matches nothing.

  THE CONTRACT (shared with theme.js's data-colors reader and the swatch
  picker): a photograph belongs to a colour when its ALT TEXT names it as
  " in <Colour>," or " in <Colour>-" — " i " covers the Danish-language alt
  texts in the source catalogue. Alt text wins because it tags EVERY photo of a
  colour; variant.featured_media points at exactly one, so it is only the
  fallback for catalogues with no alt convention at all.

  Params: media · product · color_opt_index (-1 = product has no colour option)
          · color_values (that option's values)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if color_opt_index > -1 -%}
  {%- assign mc_alt = media.alt | default: '' | downcase -%}
  {%- assign mc_tagged = false -%}
  {%- for cv in color_values -%}
    {%- assign cv_down = cv | downcase -%}
    {%- assign mc_n1 = ' in ' | append: cv_down | append: ',' -%}
    {%- assign mc_n2 = ' in ' | append: cv_down | append: '-' -%}
    {%- assign mc_n3 = ' i ' | append: cv_down | append: ',' -%}
    {%- assign mc_n4 = ' i ' | append: cv_down | append: '-' -%}
    {%- if mc_alt contains mc_n1 or mc_alt contains mc_n2 or mc_alt contains mc_n3 or mc_alt contains mc_n4 -%}
      {{- cv -}}||{%- assign mc_tagged = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- unless mc_tagged -%}
    {%- for pv in product.variants -%}
      {%- if pv.featured_media.id == media.id -%}{{- pv.options[color_opt_index] -}}||{%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}
